From 20b2aefaa86f28b9520884a9f5cdb8df0963fbf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 06:33:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08874/11362] Restore 5 dropped fabrication-gate
 determinations; correct a wrong root cause; add win-exemplar replay

RECORD REPAIR FIRST. determination-preservation-lint refused a commit because five
artifacts had lost `flagged_adversarial: True` plus their corrigendum_note and
corrigendum_pending records: experiment_1736_kanele_synth, the three
archive_v309/v310/v311 activations, and experiment_833_constraint_delta_root_cause.
Dropping that field LIFTS a quarantine, so those artifacts would have been
re-admitted to headline aggregation. HEAD still held the correct values and the
stripped versions were already STAGED, so this was one commit from publication.

Repaired per the lint's own instruction -- restore the determination fields
ALONGSIDE the new numbers -- by copying back only the keys HEAD had and the
working tree had lost. NOT by `git checkout --`, which would have restored the
determinations by discarding whatever legitimate re-run numbers those files had
gained, and which is how this guard has destroyed authored work three times.

The pending test-suite-mutation marker (pytest tests/python -q, ppid-769900) is
deleted deliberately, as that guard permits once investigated: its own
attributed_to_run was EMPTY and it flagged all 17 paths as [NOT this run], i.e.
concurrent activity. The one real rewrite inside its window was the determination
stripping above, now repaired.

Root cause unchanged: the conductor commits with --no-verify, so neither guard
runs on its commits. Second guard in two days showing that asymmetry, this time
with real data loss narrowly avoided rather than mere inconvenience.

CORRECTION. Yesterday I wrote in three places that collect_transitions "discards
win states by restarting on level-up". WRONG -- it appends the level-up
transition BEFORE restarting. The real cause, measured: a salience-biased random
walk essentially never reaches a level-up (0 of 200 steps on dc22, 0 of 200 on
cn04). The wrong claim is preserved per never-prune and corrected in
ops/known-issues.md. Acting on it would have produced a two-line change to a
restart branch that accomplished nothing.

NEW CAPABILITY. replay_win_transition() replays a banked solve from
results/arc_loop_solve_<game>.json through the game's OWN GameAdapter.apply and
returns the first level-up transition. Using the adapter's apply matters: label
dialects differ per game (dc22's ACTION6 rows carry grid/x/y, not data). Verified
live on dc22, cn04 and ls20.

WHY IT MATTERS. induce_prompt has dedicated slots for win_transition and
previous_level_complete_grid, and every offline experiment run yesterday passed
NEITHER because there was no level-up to pass. So every offline induction number
this project holds, including exp5764's 0.378 pooled held-out, was measured with
that slot empty. exp6255 measures what filling it does, paired, one induce per
arm per game.

SCOPE LIMIT, in the code and the artifact: replaying a banked solve is a
development proxy. A hidden game has no banked solve and no adapter, so the live
agent cannot get an exemplar this way; on the live path it comes from the agent's
own play and exists from level 2 onward, never level 1.

